    {
      "id": "2101672304358948992",
      "url": "https://x.com/rasbt/status/2101672304358948992",
      "author_handle": "rasbt",
      "author_name": "Sebastian Raschka",
      "post_text": "It’s easy to dismiss Jev it as “just a classifier”.\n\nBut people (me included) who have been training encoder-style models for classification for many years know they were usually special-purpose and limited in some way.\n\nThe breakthrough of Jev is that it generalizes well.\n\nAnd I’d say the secret sauce is probably more in the data than in the training algorithm. (Plus a nice API design on top of it.)",
